410 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Goblins\054 with their small build and innate tendency to run from danger\054 are surprisingly adaptable to nearly any environment\056 While often cowardly in the face of immediate threat\054 a Goblin\047s heightened sense of curiosity often leaves them running headlong into trouble\056 Unstable or unknown magic\054 unexplored caverns\054 and a chance to gather a precious trophy from a deep tomb are far more valuable to a Goblin than even their own lives\054 at times\056\n\nWhile many wild Goblins will live in caves and jungles\054 many others will live in civilizations amongst other races wherever they are permitted\056 Goblins are not seen as equals by many others and\054 as such\054 are not often found in less tolerant cities or civilizations\056 This hesitation does not come without justification\054 however\054 as many Goblins despise civilization and seek pleasure in burning and pillaging\056 Those who do not share this destructive view are often rather friendly\054 looking to entertain others with stories of grandiose adventure\056\n\nWhen upright\054 Goblins stand around 3\0476\042\056 Covered in fur with tints of blues\054 greens or even pinks\054 a Goblin prefers to run on all fours whenever possible\054 especially when climbing and scampering\056 Their eyes are often a green or brown color\054 narrowing into vertical slits to see in darkness\056 Long\054 sharp claws extend from the end of each finger giving Goblins slight defenses when cornered\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 411 0 R
     /Pg 408 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

